---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = "September 15, 2026";
const lastUpdatedISO = "2026-09-15";
---

<Layout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Learn what cookies and similar technologies N3 Global Tech uses on our website, and how you can control them."
  keywords="cookie policy, cookies, web tracking, N3 Global Tech cookies, browser cookies"
>
  <Navbar />

  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="container legal-hero__inner">
      <div class="badge badge-sky">Legal</div>
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-hero__meta">Last updated: <time datetime={lastUpdatedISO}>{lastUpdated}</time></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="legal-article">
    <div class="container legal-narrow">

      <p class="legal-lead">
        This Cookie Policy explains how N3 Global Tech ("N3 Global Tech", "N3", "we", "our", or "us") uses cookies and similar technologies when you visit <a href="https://www.n3global.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.n3global.tech</a>.
        This Cookie Policy should be read together with our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
        By using our website, you acknowledge the use of cookies and similar technologies as described in this Policy.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files placed on your computer, mobile device, or other internet-connected device by a website when you visit it. Cookies allow websites to recognise your device, store your preferences, and provide you with a more personalised experience.
      </p>
      <p>In addition to cookies, we may use similar technologies such as:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Web beacons / pixel tags:</strong> Tiny images embedded in web pages or emails that allow us to measure usage patterns and track whether emails are opened.</li>
        <li><strong>Local storage &amp; session storage:</strong> Browser-based storage mechanisms that behave similarly to cookies but are stored directly in your browser.</li>
        <li><strong>Scripts and SDKs:</strong> Code embedded on our pages that may collect data about how you interact with our site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Types of Cookies We Use</h2>

      <h3>2.1 Strictly Necessary Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        These cookies are essential for our website to function correctly. Without them, services such as page navigation, access to secure areas, and form submissions would not be possible. Because they are strictly necessary, they cannot be switched off in our systems.
      </p>
      <div class="cookie-table-wrap">
        <table class="cookie-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Cookie Name</th>
              <th>Provider</th>
              <th>Purpose</th>
              <th>Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>__vercel_live_token</code></td>
              <td>Vercel</td>
              <td>Required for infrastructure routing and server-side rendering on our hosting platform.</td>
              <td>Session</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_csrf</code></td>
              <td>N3 Global Tech</td>
              <td>Security cookie to prevent cross-site request forgery attacks on forms.</td>
              <td>Session</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>2.2 Performance &amp; Analytics Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        These cookies help us understand how visitors interact with our website. All information collected is aggregated and therefore anonymous. If you do not allow these cookies, we will not know when you have visited our site or be able to monitor its performance.
      </p>
      <div class="cookie-table-wrap">
        <table class="cookie-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Cookie Name</th>
              <th>Provider</th>
              <th>Purpose</th>
              <th>Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_ga</code></td>
              <td>Google Analytics</td>
              <td>Registers a unique ID to generate statistical data on how visitors use the website.</td>
              <td>2 years</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>_ga_*</code></td>
              <td>Google Analytics</td>
              <td>Used by Google Analytics 4 to persist session state.</td>
              <td>2 years</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>2.3 Functional Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation, such as remembering your preferences or language settings. They may be set by us or by third-party providers whose services we have added to our pages.
      </p>
      <div class="cookie-table-wrap">
        <table class="cookie-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Cookie Name</th>
              <th>Provider</th>
              <th>Purpose</th>
              <th>Duration</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>n3_cookie_consent</code></td>
              <td>N3 Global Tech</td>
              <td>Stores your cookie preferences so you are not asked again on every visit.</td>
              <td>1 year</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>2.4 Marketing &amp; Targeting Cookies</h3>
      <p>
        We currently do <strong>not</strong> use marketing or advertising cookies. We do not deploy retargeting pixels, advertising networks, or social-media tracking on our website. Should this change, we will update this Policy and obtain your explicit consent before placing any such cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        Some third-party services we use may set cookies independently. We do not control these third-party cookies. Please refer to the respective providers' privacy and cookie policies for more information:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Fonts:</strong> Used to load typography. Google may log the request as part of normal traffic. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel:</strong> Our hosting and deployment platform may set cookies for security and infrastructure purposes. See <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics:</strong> If enabled, this service collects anonymised usage data to help us improve the website. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. How Long Do Cookies Last?</h2>
      <p>Cookies fall into two broad categories based on their lifespan:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Session cookies:</strong> These are temporary and are deleted automatically when you close your browser.</li>
        <li><strong>Persistent cookies:</strong> These remain on your device for a set period of time or until you delete them. The specific duration for each cookie is shown in the tables above.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. How to Manage Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to decide whether to accept or reject non-essential cookies. You can exercise your cookie preferences in the following ways:
      </p>
      <h3>Browser Settings</h3>
      <p>Most web browsers allow you to control cookies through their settings. You can typically:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>View all cookies stored on your device and delete them individually or in bulk</li>
        <li>Block third-party cookies</li>
        <li>Block all cookies (note: this may break functionality on many websites, including ours)</li>
        <li>Use private/incognito mode to avoid storing cookies between sessions</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Browser-specific instructions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Chrome</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Mozilla Firefox</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple Safari</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Edge</a></li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Opt-Out of Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        To opt out of Google Analytics tracking specifically, you can install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Do Not Track</h2>
      <p>
        Some browsers include a "Do Not Track" (DNT) feature that signals your preference not to be tracked across websites. Because there is currently no universal standard for how websites should respond to DNT signals, our website does not currently alter its behaviour in response to DNT signals. We will continue to review this as standards evolve.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes to This Cookie Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or for legal, operational, or regulatory reasons. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page will be updated accordingly. We encourage you to review this Policy periodically to stay informed about how we use cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where changes are material, we will take reasonable steps to notify you — for example, by displaying a prominent notice on our website or by email if you have provided your contact details.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding our use of cookies or this Cookie Policy, please contact us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Company:</strong> N3 Global Tech</li>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@n3global.tech">contact@n3global.tech</a></li>
        <li><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+919188374340">+91 91883 74340</a></li>
        <li><strong>Address:</strong> N3 Global Tech, Kannur, Kerala, India</li>
        <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.n3global.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.n3global.tech</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="legal-related">
        See also: <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a>
      </p>

    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-hero {
    padding: calc(80px + 3rem) 0 2.5rem;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f8fafc 0%, #ffffff 100%);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-100);
  }
  .legal-hero__inner {
    text-align: center;
  }
  .legal-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-hero__meta {
    color: var(--gray-500);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-article {
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
  }
  .legal-narrow {
    max-width: 960px;
  }
  .legal-lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--gray-700);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-100);
  }
  .legal-narrow h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--gray-900);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .legal-narrow h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--gray-900);
  }
  .legal-narrow p,
  .legal-narrow ul {
    color: var(--gray-700);
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }
  .legal-narrow ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .legal-narrow li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-narrow a {
    color: var(--sky-700, #0369a1);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .legal-related {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gray-100);
    color: var(--gray-500);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  /* Cookie tables */
  .cookie-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--gray-100, #f1f5f9);
  }
  .cookie-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .cookie-table thead {
    background: var(--gray-50, #f8fafc);
  }
  .cookie-table th {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--gray-700, #374151);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-200, #e5e7eb);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .cookie-table td {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    color: var(--gray-700, #374151);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-100, #f1f5f9);
    vertical-align: top;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .cookie-table tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .cookie-table code {
    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    background: var(--gray-100, #f1f5f9);
    padding: 0.15em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 3px;
    color: var(--gray-800, #1f2937);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .cookie-table th,
    .cookie-table td {
      padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
